WEBVTT

00:09.509 --> 00:11.511
[fire crackling softly]

00:15.598 --> 00:18.601
[♪ somber music playing]

00:36.578 --> 00:38.580
[water sloshing lightly]

00:44.711 --> 00:46.713
[wet rag scraping lightly]

00:53.219 --> 00:55.513
[door opens, closes]

01:39.641 --> 01:42.644
♪

02:02.705 --> 02:03.998
[Tommy sighs]

02:09.963 --> 02:12.966
[♪ somber music
continues playing]

02:27.063 --> 02:28.064
[Tommy sniffles]

02:31.901 --> 02:33.528
Give Sarah my love.

02:47.584 --> 02:49.586
[water sloshing lightly]

03:04.225 --> 03:07.311
- [overlapping shouting]
- [doctor]
...multiple lacerations.

03:07.312 --> 03:10.189
- [baby crying]
- [patient grunting]

03:10.190 --> 03:12.774
[parent] My daughter,
she's five years old.

03:12.775 --> 03:15.819
[baby continues crying]

03:15.820 --> 03:18.072
[gently humming]

03:19.073 --> 03:21.075
[Ellie wheezing]

03:25.747 --> 03:27.749
[wheezing continues]

03:29.626 --> 03:32.502
[nurse] Hey. It's okay.

03:32.503 --> 03:34.088
You're in the hospital.

03:36.424 --> 03:38.301
Are you in pain?

03:39.093 --> 03:40.595
We can give you something.

03:42.263 --> 03:44.973
- [screaming]
- Ellie!

03:44.974 --> 03:47.393
- [nurse 2] Ellie! Ellie!
- [continues screaming]

03:49.520 --> 03:52.356
- [screaming]
- [voices muffled, echoing]

03:52.357 --> 03:53.482
[nurse 1] Here.

03:53.483 --> 03:55.192
[Ellie wailing]

03:55.193 --> 03:56.527
[nurse 1]
It's okay.

03:58.196 --> 04:01.115
[continues wailing]

04:05.495 --> 04:08.498
[♪ pensive theme music playing]

05:06.764 --> 05:08.391
[♪ theme concludes]

05:11.811 --> 05:13.813
[sparks buzzing]

05:14.522 --> 05:18.066
[people chattering]

05:18.067 --> 05:20.695
[♪ light music playing]

05:30.955 --> 05:32.957
[people continue chattering]

06:01.194 --> 06:03.320
[doctor]
And how would you
rate your pain?

06:03.321 --> 06:04.446
Scale of one to ten?

06:04.447 --> 06:06.407
- Nothing. Zero.
- Zero.

06:07.492 --> 06:08.993
Can't ask for much more
than that.

06:10.036 --> 06:12.372
Okay.
One last PFT.

06:13.414 --> 06:15.957
[blowing forcefully]

06:15.958 --> 06:17.125
Pff, look at that.

06:17.126 --> 06:20.003
Yeah.
Wow, alright.

06:20.004 --> 06:21.130
Today's the day.

06:22.131 --> 06:23.632
- So, can I just--
- Almost.

06:23.633 --> 06:25.175
Uh, I just need you
to see one more person,

06:25.176 --> 06:27.219
then you're good to go.

06:27.220 --> 06:29.138
[sighs]

06:30.556 --> 06:32.642
Oh, for fuck's sake.

06:34.227 --> 06:36.353
- How are you doing?
- Fine.

06:36.354 --> 06:38.647
If you say it that fast,
it kind of implies you're not.

06:38.648 --> 06:40.649
Okay, ask me again.

06:40.650 --> 06:42.025
How are you doing, Ellie?

06:42.026 --> 06:44.694
Hmm, give me a moment.

06:44.695 --> 06:47.697
It's really complicated
'cause, you know, feelings.

06:47.698 --> 06:49.157
Okay.

06:49.158 --> 06:51.577
Oh, come on, man,
I've been stuck in here since...

06:55.581 --> 06:58.166
Yeah, I miss him.
Uh, he meant a lot to me.

06:58.167 --> 07:00.752
So, yeah.
Upset and sad.

07:00.753 --> 07:02.546
[Gail] Of course.

07:02.547 --> 07:05.006
But I was actually wondering
about New Year's Eve.

07:05.007 --> 07:07.676
You two got into it
at the dance.

07:07.677 --> 07:09.512
Was that the last time
you spoke to him?

07:11.347 --> 07:13.558
Mm-hmm. Yeah.

07:15.101 --> 07:18.353
When I got home,
he was on the porch,

07:18.354 --> 07:22.024
and I should've talked to him,
but I didn't.

07:23.025 --> 07:26.111
- Do you regret that?
- Yeah, of course.

07:26.112 --> 07:30.031
But your final moment
with someone

07:30.032 --> 07:32.868
doesn't define
your whole time with them.

07:32.869 --> 07:35.288
It shouldn't,
but it often does.

07:37.874 --> 07:40.668
In my last moment with Joel,
he said he

07:41.794 --> 07:42.920
wronged you.

07:43.921 --> 07:45.047
Maybe bad.

07:49.051 --> 07:51.429
What is it that he said
that he did?

07:52.430 --> 07:55.016
[Gail] Well, that's the thing.
It didn't really make sense.

07:55.850 --> 07:57.894
He said, "I saved her."

08:00.354 --> 08:02.481
He saved me a lot of times.

08:02.482 --> 08:05.901
Yeah, I would think so.
But that's not wronging someone.

08:05.902 --> 08:08.362
[Ellie]
Hmm. That's weird.

08:09.530 --> 08:10.948
No idea what he meant.

08:12.283 --> 08:14.785
I don't feel wronged.

08:15.953 --> 08:18.288
[sighs]
Man, I wish I could have
let him off the hook

08:18.289 --> 08:20.541
for whatever it was
he was talking about.

08:22.543 --> 08:26.171
I guess I'll have to let myself
off the hook for that.

08:26.172 --> 08:27.465
[scoffs]

08:28.299 --> 08:29.758
Well, you really
are doing good.

08:29.759 --> 08:31.343
[Ellie chuckles]

08:31.344 --> 08:34.429
Shit, if everyone
were as healthy as you,

08:34.430 --> 08:36.515
what would I do
for weed and booze?

08:36.516 --> 08:38.683
I wouldn't worry, Gail,
there's still a lot of
fucked up people

08:38.684 --> 08:40.143
- in this town.
- Yeah.

08:40.144 --> 08:41.937
But not you, though.

08:41.938 --> 08:44.023
[chuckles]

08:55.660 --> 08:58.663
[♪ gentle music playing]

09:01.082 --> 09:03.084
[people chattering]

09:10.049 --> 09:12.051
[birdsong]

09:16.180 --> 09:19.934
[♪ gentle music continues]

09:33.614 --> 09:35.074
[door closes]

09:36.075 --> 09:38.077
[floor creaking softly]

10:05.313 --> 10:07.315
[door creaking softly]

10:27.168 --> 10:29.170
[door creaking open]

11:02.912 --> 11:05.915
[♪ somber music playing]

11:27.478 --> 11:28.729
[gun clicks]

11:37.071 --> 11:40.449
♪

12:21.365 --> 12:23.367
[sniffling, sobbing]

12:37.047 --> 12:39.049
[sniffling, sobbing continue]

12:40.426 --> 12:41.510
[Dina] Ellie?

12:42.553 --> 12:43.804
[door closes]

12:44.805 --> 12:46.348
[sighs] Fuck.

12:47.391 --> 12:48.893
[sniffling]

12:51.854 --> 12:53.814
Yeah, I'm coming.

12:56.025 --> 12:57.692
[sniffling]

12:57.693 --> 12:59.069
[door closes]

13:03.824 --> 13:05.826
[footsteps approaching]

13:08.454 --> 13:10.539
[Dina]
I went to the hospital.

13:11.457 --> 13:13.374
When'd they let you out?

13:13.375 --> 13:16.003
- Thirty minutes ago.
- Nice.

13:17.254 --> 13:18.755
They made me talk to Gail.

13:18.756 --> 13:19.965
Oh.

13:24.345 --> 13:26.221
I never said--

13:26.222 --> 13:28.556
I should have said
thank you

13:28.557 --> 13:30.433
for all those times
you came to visit.

13:30.434 --> 13:32.101
Ah, that's okay.

13:32.102 --> 13:33.561
You would have done
the same for me.

13:33.562 --> 13:36.190
- Yeah, maybe not as often.
- Yeah, no, probably not.

13:38.484 --> 13:40.735
- I made you cookies.
- Oh?

13:40.736 --> 13:42.737
- Just 'cause?
- Uh, no.

13:42.738 --> 13:44.532
This is a peace offering.

13:47.076 --> 13:48.869
Because I'm about
to make you angry.

13:54.208 --> 13:55.709
In the hospital...

13:57.086 --> 14:01.589
when you asked me
about that day...

14:01.590 --> 14:04.385
I told you I didn't learn
anything useful.

14:06.220 --> 14:07.680
That wasn't true.

14:09.849 --> 14:13.811
I know most of their names,
and I know where they're from.

14:14.728 --> 14:16.104
Please, just listen.

14:16.105 --> 14:17.772
The doctors told me
not to upset you.

14:17.773 --> 14:19.858
- I don't give a fuck.
- And I knew that if I told you

14:19.859 --> 14:21.651
where they were,
you'd just start
pulling your tubes out

14:21.652 --> 14:23.528
and crawling on your hands
and knees to get there.

14:23.529 --> 14:25.406
I don't give a fuck.

14:26.490 --> 14:30.286
You cost us time.
You let them get away.

14:32.872 --> 14:34.789
First of all...

14:34.790 --> 14:37.458
this town was wreckage
and funerals for weeks.

14:37.459 --> 14:39.878
Nobody was gonna
go after anyone.

14:39.879 --> 14:42.338
And then it occurred to me,
if you wanna find someone,

14:42.339 --> 14:44.967
and the only thing
you know about them
is where they're gonna end up...

14:47.595 --> 14:49.305
maybe let them get there.

14:57.938 --> 14:59.565
I loved him too, you know.

15:08.157 --> 15:10.159
[Dina inhales deeply]

15:14.580 --> 15:15.706
[sniffling]

15:22.463 --> 15:23.756
[Dina sighing]

15:39.188 --> 15:41.357
Okay,
let's start with names.

15:42.566 --> 15:45.693
The dark-haired guy was Manny.
The other guy was Owen.

15:45.694 --> 15:47.528
The girl with the dark hair
and the bald one,

15:47.529 --> 15:49.405
one of them's named Nora.
I'm not sure which.

15:49.406 --> 15:50.783
The girl with the braid?

15:51.825 --> 15:54.328
- Abby.
- [whispering] Abby.

15:57.790 --> 15:59.124
Where are they from?

16:00.042 --> 16:01.669
I saw a patch on a backpack.

16:03.087 --> 16:05.255
Yellow triangle,
wolf's head...

16:06.423 --> 16:08.549
and the letters W-L-F.

16:08.550 --> 16:10.718
And then, I remembered
a story Eugene told me

16:10.719 --> 16:12.261
from back
when he was a Firefly.

16:12.262 --> 16:13.930
He said that there were
these small regional groups

16:13.931 --> 16:15.390
in the West
all trying to fight FEDRA,

16:15.391 --> 16:18.393
and how stupid it was that
they didn't just join together.

16:18.394 --> 16:22.231
One of those groups was
the Washington Liberation Front.

16:24.608 --> 16:26.317
Out of Seattle.

16:26.318 --> 16:28.403
[Ellie]
W-L-F. Wolf.

16:28.404 --> 16:29.571
Fucking morons.

16:30.864 --> 16:33.241
- Did he say
how small they were?
- No.

16:33.242 --> 16:35.410
But seeing as how no one's
ever mentioned them since,

16:35.411 --> 16:37.579
I'm guessing small enough
for us to handle.

16:39.707 --> 16:41.082
Who else knows?

16:41.083 --> 16:42.584
Just us.

16:44.837 --> 16:47.256
I wasn't gonna tell
anyone before you.

17:06.900 --> 17:08.277
[with mouth full]
So, now what?

17:11.030 --> 17:14.241
[cow mooing, grunting]

17:15.909 --> 17:17.244
[gate creaking open]

17:18.370 --> 17:20.372
[chickens clucking]

17:21.915 --> 17:23.042
[Ellie] Well?

17:24.043 --> 17:25.501
I gotta think about this.

17:25.502 --> 17:27.795
Think about what?
Let's fucking get these guys.

17:27.796 --> 17:29.881
Ellie, it ain't that simple.

17:29.882 --> 17:31.966
The town is still recovering.

17:31.967 --> 17:33.634
- So are you.
- Uh, we get where
you're coming from--

17:33.635 --> 17:35.011
No, we don't get
where you're coming from.

17:35.012 --> 17:36.345
I don't get where
you're coming from.

17:36.346 --> 17:38.056
If it had been you,
Joel would be halfway to Seattle

17:38.057 --> 17:39.974
- before the sun came up.
- He'd be halfway to Seattle

17:39.975 --> 17:41.976
to save my life.

17:41.977 --> 17:43.978
But when we lost people, no.

17:43.979 --> 17:46.147
It would just break him
like it was his fault.

17:46.148 --> 17:47.565
I saw that time
and time again.

17:47.566 --> 17:50.193
And don't talk to me
like I didn't know him.

17:50.194 --> 17:51.528
He was my brother.

17:57.159 --> 18:00.704
Listen, I'm not sayin'
you shouldn't do this.

18:01.705 --> 18:03.331
But if we're gonna put
a posse together,

18:03.332 --> 18:05.708
we gotta do it right,
which means taking it to Maria.

18:05.709 --> 18:08.002
Yes, it's fuckin' necessary.

18:08.003 --> 18:09.670
She's gonna want
a council meeting,

18:09.671 --> 18:10.880
open it up to the town.

18:10.881 --> 18:13.050
Everyone who wants
to get heard gets heard.

18:14.259 --> 18:15.761
But you'll back us, right?

18:16.512 --> 18:17.805
Of course, I will.

18:21.266 --> 18:22.351
Come here.

18:28.774 --> 18:31.692
And you, you hold out
information on me again,

18:31.693 --> 18:34.279
you got rendering detail
for a month.

18:36.448 --> 18:37.449
Alright.

18:41.495 --> 18:42.579
Ellie.

18:45.541 --> 18:48.001
We buried our dead
ten miles south of town.

18:48.752 --> 18:50.295
If you want to visit him.

18:53.048 --> 18:54.967
When we're on our way
to Seattle.

19:00.097 --> 19:02.099
[chickens clucking]

19:09.398 --> 19:11.566
[birds chirping]

19:11.567 --> 19:14.570
[♪ dramatic music playing]

19:22.119 --> 19:23.871
[crow cawing]

19:25.414 --> 19:27.416
[animals chittering]

19:34.089 --> 19:36.383
[whistling]

19:40.429 --> 19:41.930
[whistling]

19:43.015 --> 19:45.017
[whistling response]

19:51.815 --> 19:52.983
Well?

19:54.443 --> 19:57.778
"No one following.
All clear. Keep moving."

19:57.779 --> 19:59.155
Good.

19:59.156 --> 20:02.117
Once we get resettled,
I'll teach you to whistle.

20:05.329 --> 20:07.622
Why can't you tell me
where we're going?

20:07.623 --> 20:09.499
'Cause we don't know yet.

20:10.751 --> 20:12.835
I've told you
the reason we're going.

20:12.836 --> 20:16.964
I know, but why can't she
just keep us safe?

20:16.965 --> 20:18.258
The Prophet?

20:19.635 --> 20:21.552
She's been dead
ten years, Constance.

20:21.553 --> 20:23.512
I wouldn't count on her
to help.

20:23.513 --> 20:26.307
But Ezra said
the Prophet is eternal.

20:26.308 --> 20:29.144
Well, she is, in a way.

20:29.811 --> 20:31.312
A prophet isn't magic.

20:31.313 --> 20:34.899
They're just people that see
truths hidden from others

20:34.900 --> 20:37.402
and share that truth,
no matter what the cost.

20:38.570 --> 20:40.655
So it was with our Prophet.

20:40.656 --> 20:42.240
[group]
So it was.

20:42.241 --> 20:44.659
That's how we keep
her spirit alive.

20:44.660 --> 20:47.912
Follow her words,
we obey her teachings,

20:47.913 --> 20:49.790
but we keep ourselves safe.

20:53.418 --> 20:55.671
Then, can I have a hammer?

20:59.341 --> 21:00.425
Alright.

21:03.553 --> 21:06.430
Tell me, you feel safer?

21:06.431 --> 21:07.641
[chuckles] Yes.

21:08.642 --> 21:10.059
Good.

21:10.060 --> 21:12.728
Understand,
what we're giving you now,

21:12.729 --> 21:15.357
will keep you far, far safer
than a hammer.

21:17.943 --> 21:19.444
Distance.

21:20.570 --> 21:23.407
- From home.
- From war.

21:25.826 --> 21:27.411
[whistling in distance]

21:30.080 --> 21:32.040
[whistling]

21:33.333 --> 21:34.792
[whistling in distance]

21:34.793 --> 21:36.378
[Jacob]
Take cover! Go!

21:38.171 --> 21:40.173
[♪ tense music playing]

21:53.562 --> 21:54.730
Demons?

21:56.732 --> 21:57.941
Wolves.

22:00.068 --> 22:01.110
- [punches thudding]
- [Ellie grunting]

22:01.111 --> 22:02.236
[Jesse] Alright.

22:02.237 --> 22:04.572
Good, but rotate.
More.

22:04.573 --> 22:07.742
Now, the right side.
Just the right side.

22:07.743 --> 22:09.076
Come on, man,
that side hurts more.

22:09.077 --> 22:10.953
I noticed.

22:10.954 --> 22:12.121
- Come on.
- Okay.

22:12.122 --> 22:13.497
[Ellie grunting]

22:13.498 --> 22:14.832
Harder.

22:14.833 --> 22:16.167
Harder! Let's go!

22:16.168 --> 22:17.501
Last five.

22:17.502 --> 22:19.920
[punches thudding]

22:19.921 --> 22:22.506
There it is, okay.
Done for the day.

22:22.507 --> 22:24.092
- [Ellie] [panting] Okay.
- [Velcro tearing]

22:25.010 --> 22:26.427
So, what'd you think?

22:26.428 --> 22:27.845
Well, for someone
who sat on their ass

22:27.846 --> 22:30.431
for three months,
I'm pleasantly surprised.

22:30.432 --> 22:32.350
- Yeah?
- Push-ups?

22:32.351 --> 22:34.477
Yeah, and crunches
when they weren't looking.

22:34.478 --> 22:36.937
Yeah, that'll do it.
A few more weeks,

22:36.938 --> 22:38.689
and you'll be right back
to where you were before.

22:38.690 --> 22:40.316
Nice.

22:40.317 --> 22:42.193
Which is 80% of where
you should have been.

22:42.194 --> 22:44.071
- Whatever. Fuck you.
- [bag chains rattling]

22:47.366 --> 22:50.534
So, I heard you're on
the council now.

22:50.535 --> 22:53.204
- Yep.
- [sighs]

22:53.205 --> 22:55.415
So, you know about
the meeting coming up?

22:56.917 --> 22:58.377
I know about the meeting
coming up.

23:00.379 --> 23:02.339
Can I count on you?

23:04.257 --> 23:05.841
I can't discuss
upcoming votes.

23:05.842 --> 23:07.968
Seriously? It's me.

23:07.969 --> 23:11.013
- I know.
- Dude, you were there.

23:11.014 --> 23:12.474
I know that too.

23:13.517 --> 23:14.601
Gotta go.

23:16.186 --> 23:17.521
[under breath]
Oh, my God.

23:19.147 --> 23:20.898
[Jesse] Ellie.

23:20.899 --> 23:22.358
The council won't
make up their mind

23:22.359 --> 23:23.984
until we hear people speak.

23:23.985 --> 23:26.153
So, here's a little advice.

23:26.154 --> 23:28.572
Organize your thoughts,
write them down,

23:28.573 --> 23:30.157
and then read 'em
out loud tomorrow.

23:30.158 --> 23:31.909
Okay, yeah,
'cause I'm stupid.

23:31.910 --> 23:33.870
'Cause you're angry, Ellie.

23:35.163 --> 23:36.915
And no one's gonna vote
for angry.

23:39.626 --> 23:41.628
[breathing heavily]

23:44.840 --> 23:47.341
[Scott] Which is why I keep
saying we need to invest

23:47.342 --> 23:50.094
more in turkeys
and less in chickens.

23:50.095 --> 23:53.347
And that brings me back
to my earlier point about corn.

23:53.348 --> 23:55.516
Corn, some of you
have heard me say,

23:55.517 --> 23:59.270
is not the easiest crop to grow,
but it is among the fastest.

23:59.271 --> 24:02.189
You can plot a graph
that shows ease and resources

24:02.190 --> 24:04.066
versus time to harvest
and get a li--

24:04.067 --> 24:07.612
Scott, I'm sorry, but we gotta
keep you on target here.

24:08.947 --> 24:11.073
But it's an open meeting.
The bylaws say that--

24:11.074 --> 24:12.616
Maybe we should stick
to what everyone else

24:12.617 --> 24:14.243
came here to discuss.

24:14.244 --> 24:17.246
I don't really have an opinion
on the Seattle thing.

24:17.247 --> 24:19.124
Okay. Thank you.

24:20.208 --> 24:21.460
So, that was Scott.

24:22.252 --> 24:23.711
Next is Rachel.

24:23.712 --> 24:25.129
- [people murmuring]
- [Rachel] Yeah, Joel meant

24:25.130 --> 24:27.047
- so much to so many of us.
- [baby fussing]

24:27.048 --> 24:29.049
- [attendee] Can't hear you.
- [Rachel grunting]

24:29.050 --> 24:31.218
- [baby crying]
- Can you take him, please?

24:31.219 --> 24:33.137
[partner] Yeah.
Okay, here we go.

24:33.138 --> 24:35.599
[baby fussing]

24:40.854 --> 24:43.648
I said that Joel meant
so much to so many of us.

24:44.816 --> 24:46.151
But he wasn't the only one.

24:47.319 --> 24:49.112
I lost my sister that day.

24:50.113 --> 24:52.281
A lot of people in here
buried family.

24:52.282 --> 24:55.660
And now, you wanna send, what,
you're saying 16 of our best?

24:57.746 --> 25:00.289
Well, while they're gone,
who's gonna be on the wall
if Raiders come?

25:00.290 --> 25:03.584
A wall that's barely mended.
And none of you up there

25:03.585 --> 25:05.921
can promise us
that all 16 will come back.

25:06.505 --> 25:10.550
So, my heart is with you,
Tommy and Ellie.

25:11.551 --> 25:13.887
We are too hurt,
and it is too soon.

25:15.138 --> 25:16.556
[Maria]
Thank you, Rachel.

25:18.225 --> 25:20.684
[people murmuring]

25:20.685 --> 25:22.187
[Maria]
Next is Carlisle.

25:23.188 --> 25:25.606
[clearing throat]

25:25.607 --> 25:27.608
I'll be quick. [sighs]

25:27.609 --> 25:29.945
'Cause this one's simple to me.

25:30.862 --> 25:33.782
People came and killed Joel.

25:34.950 --> 25:37.327
So, why wouldn't we wanna
take our vengeance?

25:38.328 --> 25:41.122
Well, because we're not
supposed to.

25:42.874 --> 25:46.126
Forgive and be forgiven.

25:46.127 --> 25:48.755
No grudges.
No revenge.

25:49.297 --> 25:51.131
And I'm not even a Christian.

25:51.132 --> 25:53.717
I've always seen
the wisdom in that.

25:53.718 --> 25:56.845
That's what separates us
from the Raiders

25:56.846 --> 25:59.139
and the murderers.

25:59.140 --> 26:00.809
Our capacity for mercy.

26:01.977 --> 26:04.144
Those sons of bitches
don't deserve our mercy.

26:04.145 --> 26:05.479
[people murmuring]

26:05.480 --> 26:07.022
[Carlisle] Well, of course
they don't deserve it.

26:07.023 --> 26:09.359
- That's what makes it mercy.
- Well, to hell with that.

26:10.402 --> 26:12.194
And to hell with you
for saying it, Carlisle.

26:12.195 --> 26:13.362
- [Maria] Seth, sit down.
- No.

26:13.363 --> 26:15.489
- [Maria] You're not on the list.
- No!

26:15.490 --> 26:17.534
What the hell are we
all talking about here?

26:18.743 --> 26:21.161
Boo-hoo, it's not fair.

26:21.162 --> 26:23.163
What, we gotta
forgive everybody
when they show up

26:23.164 --> 26:25.165
and piss in our eye?

26:25.166 --> 26:27.501
They came into our house.

26:27.502 --> 26:29.337
They took one of ours.

26:30.046 --> 26:32.715
My God, somebody
shoots your brother,

26:32.716 --> 26:34.842
you wanna take the locks
off your doors?

26:34.843 --> 26:35.969
Grow up!

26:36.886 --> 26:38.763
You idiots, they'll come back.

26:39.598 --> 26:42.350
They'll come back because
we didn't make 'em pay.

26:43.018 --> 26:45.478
And when they come back,
they'll be laughing.

26:47.606 --> 26:49.149
And you'll all deserve it.

26:50.525 --> 26:54.070
Bunch of goddamn victims.

27:04.414 --> 27:05.957
- [attendee clearing throat]
- [Maria sighs]

27:08.501 --> 27:09.586
Ellie?

27:17.385 --> 27:18.386
[chair scraping]

27:21.973 --> 27:23.975
- [Ellie clearing throat]
- [paper rustling]

27:28.521 --> 27:31.398
[clearing throat]
I normally don't
write things down

27:31.399 --> 27:33.817
because I normally
don't think before I talk,

27:33.818 --> 27:36.904
which has gotten me
in trouble before, a lot,

27:36.905 --> 27:41.075
and it's cost me in ways that
sometimes couldn't be undone.

27:41.076 --> 27:42.910
But I can't afford that
right now,

27:42.911 --> 27:45.664
because I know
what I'm asking is a lot.

27:46.373 --> 27:49.291
I'm asking us to risk
more people and resources,

27:49.292 --> 27:51.335
and at the worst
possible time.

27:51.336 --> 27:55.506
And I want everyone to know,
it's not because I want revenge.

27:55.507 --> 27:57.925
It's not.
It's not about revenge.

27:57.926 --> 28:00.804
What I want is what you
used to give people.

28:01.805 --> 28:03.306
I want justice.

28:04.641 --> 28:08.102
Because it's either that,
or we do nothing.

28:08.103 --> 28:11.188
That's what everyone else
out there is going to do for us.

28:11.189 --> 28:12.606
Nothing.

28:12.607 --> 28:15.317
A whole world of people
who won't lift a finger

28:15.318 --> 28:18.196
if something bad
happens to me or you.

28:19.781 --> 28:22.324
We have a word
for these people.

28:22.325 --> 28:24.201
They're called strangers.

28:24.202 --> 28:27.037
Well, I don't think that
we're strangers to each other.

28:27.038 --> 28:29.540
And I want to know
that I can count on you.

28:29.541 --> 28:31.834
And I swear,
if someone hurts any of you

28:31.835 --> 28:35.045
or the people you love,
you can count on me.

28:35.046 --> 28:37.382
That's what holds
all this together.

28:38.800 --> 28:41.344
Not potluck dinners
or New Year's Eve dances.

28:42.345 --> 28:45.139
Definitely not a wall,
because that thing
got busted through.

28:45.140 --> 28:46.975
But Jackson is still here.

28:50.311 --> 28:52.479
I'll accept whatever
the council decides.

28:52.480 --> 28:55.567
But I am asking you,
please...

28:56.901 --> 28:59.612
do what it takes to see
that justice is done.

29:01.322 --> 29:04.576
Not for me.
Not even for Joel.

29:05.827 --> 29:10.874
I am asking you,
please, do it for us.

29:15.795 --> 29:16.963
Thank you.

29:17.964 --> 29:20.967
[people murmuring]

29:26.389 --> 29:28.432
The council will now
vote on the proposal

29:28.433 --> 29:31.393
to send a party
of 16 citizens to Seattle

29:31.394 --> 29:34.939
to find the people who killed
Joel and execute them.

29:37.150 --> 29:39.360
[murmuring continues]

29:57.420 --> 29:59.130
[Maria] Amy-Beth?

30:03.259 --> 30:04.260
Yes.

30:06.262 --> 30:07.263
No.

30:08.973 --> 30:10.099
Yes.

30:12.477 --> 30:13.603
No.

30:15.271 --> 30:16.356
No.

30:17.857 --> 30:18.858
Yes.

30:20.568 --> 30:21.611
No.

30:23.905 --> 30:24.948
No.

30:26.366 --> 30:27.492
No.

30:28.952 --> 30:29.994
No.

30:32.080 --> 30:33.331
No.

30:36.167 --> 30:39.921
The vote is 8 to 3.
The proposal is rejected.

30:41.256 --> 30:43.383
[murmuring continues]

30:45.677 --> 30:47.261
Adjourned.

30:47.262 --> 30:49.722
[people chattering]

31:01.401 --> 31:03.862
[chattering continues]

31:07.448 --> 31:09.701
[cheering and applause]

31:12.287 --> 31:14.497
[Gail]
Here we go, nine.
Here we go.

31:16.791 --> 31:19.001
[coach]
Grab the ball!

31:19.002 --> 31:21.045
- [Gail] Attaboy, nine!
- [spectators shouting]

31:22.046 --> 31:23.881
- [crowd] Ooh!
- Oh, shit.

31:23.882 --> 31:25.800
I didn't know you were a fan.

31:26.509 --> 31:29.177
Hell, yeah!
I had Tigers season tickets.

31:29.178 --> 31:30.512
[coach]
Get in the game, Charlie.

31:30.513 --> 31:33.348
This actually isn't that far off
from the '03 squad.

31:33.349 --> 31:35.517
[parent]
Louie, stand up! Stand up!

31:35.518 --> 31:38.729
You want a beer?
I get them from Marshall.

31:38.730 --> 31:40.773
[people chattering]

31:43.693 --> 31:46.362
- [bottle cap popping]
- [bottles clinking]

31:51.659 --> 31:54.077
I spotted you in the crowd
at the meeting today.

31:54.078 --> 31:56.039
- Mm.
- Yeah.

31:57.624 --> 31:59.917
And I thought to myself,

31:59.918 --> 32:02.420
she's probably been extra busy
these last few weeks.

32:03.421 --> 32:04.838
Brutal.

32:04.839 --> 32:06.548
And I'm supposed to see
a shrink myself,

32:06.549 --> 32:08.926
you know,
to process it all, it's...

32:08.927 --> 32:10.219
I'm the only one here.

32:10.970 --> 32:14.264
- So, what do you do, then?
- Oh, well, I'm an alcoholic.

32:14.265 --> 32:16.683
And I smoke
as much weed as I can.

32:16.684 --> 32:19.436
You know,
complete fuckin' disaster.

32:19.437 --> 32:21.564
But you're not here
'cause you're worried about me.

32:21.981 --> 32:24.691
[coach] Two outs, guys,
two outs. Look alive!

32:24.692 --> 32:25.860
I don't know.

32:26.277 --> 32:28.196
- [baseball bat thumps]
- [people cheering]

32:28.613 --> 32:30.156
You see things
that others don't.

32:32.158 --> 32:35.077
I'm nervous she's gonna do
somethin' stupid.

32:35.078 --> 32:36.912
What, you didn't
believe her speech?

32:36.913 --> 32:39.624
- Did you?
- Course not. She's a liar.

32:40.458 --> 32:42.709
Well, there's a difference
between lyin' and being a liar.

32:42.710 --> 32:45.254
Oh, I know.
And that one? Liar.

32:46.089 --> 32:47.381
There was maybe one person

32:47.382 --> 32:49.342
she told the truth to,
and he's...

32:51.844 --> 32:53.720
But we can agree
to disagree about that.

32:53.721 --> 32:55.389
[cheering and applause
in distance]

32:55.390 --> 32:59.726
What matters is you're afraid.
So, let's talk about it.

32:59.727 --> 33:02.021
Okay.
Free of charge.

33:05.191 --> 33:08.444
I just don't want her to go down
the same paths that Joel did.

33:11.406 --> 33:13.741
Comin' up with
justifications and such.

33:15.868 --> 33:18.286
All he was really doin'
was lashin' out.

33:18.287 --> 33:21.916
So, you think she might have
learned that behavior from him?

33:24.085 --> 33:25.627
[coach]
There it is! Keep it up.

33:25.628 --> 33:28.505
Turns out nurture
can only do this much.

33:28.506 --> 33:30.590
The rest is nature.

33:30.591 --> 33:33.177
If she's on a path,
it's not one
that Joel put her on.

33:34.470 --> 33:36.096
No. No.

33:36.097 --> 33:38.181
I think they were
walking side by side

33:38.182 --> 33:39.684
from the very start.

33:42.979 --> 33:45.147
Tommy, I get it.

33:45.148 --> 33:48.191
You inherited her, and you
wanna keep her out of trouble.

33:48.192 --> 33:50.987
Take it from a psychotherapist
of 40 years.

33:51.988 --> 33:53.364
Some people just...

33:57.493 --> 33:59.829
Some people just can't be saved.

34:01.122 --> 34:04.125
[cheering and applause
continue in distance]

34:20.808 --> 34:22.101
[knocking]

34:27.023 --> 34:28.231
[loud knocking]

34:28.232 --> 34:30.568
- Who is it?
- Dina.

34:34.489 --> 34:35.490
Hey.

34:36.699 --> 34:39.826
Uh, I'm just going to bed.

34:39.827 --> 34:42.997
[Dina] No, I-- I don't think
that is where you're going.

34:48.628 --> 34:51.464
- Are you alone?
- I'm alone.

35:00.014 --> 35:01.348
Get in.

35:01.349 --> 35:03.767
[sighing]
Oh, Christ.

35:03.768 --> 35:05.352
Please don't try
and talk me out of this.

35:05.353 --> 35:06.896
Oh, you think
that's why I'm here?

35:07.939 --> 35:10.817
So, uh, what's your plan?

35:12.235 --> 35:14.194
Go to Seattle and kill Abby.

35:14.195 --> 35:15.655
Mm. What route?

35:16.322 --> 35:18.240
Northwest.

35:18.241 --> 35:21.701
And is that all guns, or do you
have medical supplies in there?

35:21.702 --> 35:22.745
No?

35:24.038 --> 35:26.540
Well, better not land
weird on an ankle

35:26.541 --> 35:30.043
or get a fever on your
well-charted path "northwest."

35:30.044 --> 35:32.046
Okay, so what
am I supposed to do?

35:38.302 --> 35:39.636
Stay off the highways.

35:39.637 --> 35:41.555
Steer clear of cities
or settlements.

35:41.556 --> 35:43.598
First stage is through
the national forest.

35:43.599 --> 35:46.977
Once we're out, we follow
the Snake River Canyon,

35:46.978 --> 35:48.562
then break off through
the Snoqualmie Pass.

35:48.563 --> 35:49.938
Snoqualmie?

35:49.939 --> 35:52.482
Yeah. Snoqualmie.

35:52.483 --> 35:54.067
Approach Seattle
from the east,

35:54.068 --> 35:55.902
then reassess
based on what we find.

35:55.903 --> 35:58.613
Provisions.
Travel light, but smart.

35:58.614 --> 36:00.657
Winter coats for beds,
jackets for blankets.

36:00.658 --> 36:02.993
First aid kits,
batteries, bear spray.

36:02.994 --> 36:05.037
Now, handguns.
What are you bringing?

36:07.165 --> 36:09.083
- Is that Joel's?
- Mm-hmm.

36:10.626 --> 36:12.252
So, that's what you're
gonna kill her with?

36:12.253 --> 36:14.421
- Fuckin' right.
- Then, save it for that.

36:14.422 --> 36:15.923
It's slow and kicks like hell.

36:18.217 --> 36:20.927
Really?
Shoot your damn ass off?

36:20.928 --> 36:23.430
Ah, I've heard that before.

36:23.431 --> 36:25.932
We'll want at least
100 shells apiece,
plus 50 rifle rounds.

36:25.933 --> 36:28.435
Bring any long gun you want,
as long as it's scoped.

36:28.436 --> 36:30.020
Uh, chlorine tablets, a pan,

36:30.021 --> 36:31.271
and something
to keep Shimmer dry.

36:31.272 --> 36:32.939
- Just Shimmer?
- Yeah.

36:32.940 --> 36:34.774
We share a horse.
Fewer resources.

36:34.775 --> 36:38.362
Everything else is what
you'd figure, except this.

36:39.822 --> 36:41.781
- Boots.
- Hm?

36:41.782 --> 36:44.451
Love the Converse.
Respect your consistency.

36:44.452 --> 36:46.620
But you're not crossing
open country in fuckin' Chucks.

36:46.621 --> 36:48.997
- I've done it before.
- No Chucks. Questions?

36:48.998 --> 36:51.666
Yeah, one. How the fuck
are we gonna get all of this?

36:51.667 --> 36:52.960
I know a guy.

36:53.961 --> 36:56.630
Oh, no. No, don't tell me
you told Jesse, please.

36:56.631 --> 36:58.965
Captain Wyoming?
No.

36:58.966 --> 37:00.967
I love the man,
but he's a little uptight

37:00.968 --> 37:02.302
about rules and shit.

37:02.303 --> 37:04.554
Wear all the clothes
you're gonna bring,

37:04.555 --> 37:06.056
fill your pockets with ammo.

37:06.057 --> 37:07.891
Everything else needs to fit
inside a holster

37:07.892 --> 37:09.309
or your backpack.

37:09.310 --> 37:12.520
We'll meet by the old east gate,
3:00 a.m.

37:12.521 --> 37:14.065
- Mm.
- 3:00 a.m.

37:15.107 --> 37:16.192
Hey.

37:19.820 --> 37:21.072
Thank you.

37:23.449 --> 37:25.867
You know, you could have
just asked.

37:25.868 --> 37:27.954
No, I actually didn't know that.

37:30.790 --> 37:32.124
Now you do.

37:39.173 --> 37:40.924
[crickets chirping]

37:40.925 --> 37:42.842
[owl hooting]

37:42.843 --> 37:44.887
[leaves rustling]

37:48.975 --> 37:50.977
[rustling continues]

37:58.359 --> 37:59.986
[Shimmer chortles]

38:00.903 --> 38:03.155
[footsteps approaching]

38:06.242 --> 38:07.535
[Seth sighs]

38:09.036 --> 38:10.496
Trade.

38:12.248 --> 38:14.125
It's better. Trade.

38:32.351 --> 38:34.394
How'd you get her out?

38:34.395 --> 38:36.646
Jeanine's night watch
at the stables.

38:36.647 --> 38:38.732
She's sympathetic
to our cause.

38:38.733 --> 38:40.066
"Our cause"?

38:40.067 --> 38:42.570
You're the one that gave
the "us" speech, not me.

38:44.655 --> 38:47.407
Saddlebags are filled with stuff
I had squirreled away.

38:47.408 --> 38:49.409
Two weeks' worth of hardtack,
bandages,

38:49.410 --> 38:51.494
alcohol, meds, batteries.
I'd come with you,

38:51.495 --> 38:53.830
but I caught
some friendly fire
on New Year's Day.

38:53.831 --> 38:56.625
- You sure it was friendly?
- Jesus Christ.

38:57.168 --> 38:59.211
We got ten minutes
before a patrol comes by.

39:00.212 --> 39:01.464
Let's get you going.

39:07.261 --> 39:09.763
[latch unlocking]

39:09.764 --> 39:11.807
[door thumping, creaking open]

39:18.064 --> 39:21.067
[♪ soft music playing]

39:37.875 --> 39:39.168
[Shimmer chortles]

39:47.760 --> 39:49.762
[gate creaking]

39:55.101 --> 39:57.103
[♪ music fades out]

40:01.690 --> 40:03.692
[wind blowing softly]

40:11.575 --> 40:13.285
[Shimmer softly grunting]

40:26.006 --> 40:29.009
[♪ somber music playing]

41:16.682 --> 41:18.267
[chuckles softly]

41:38.120 --> 41:39.955
[sighs deeply]

41:43.792 --> 41:46.795
[♪ somber music
continues playing]

42:22.081 --> 42:25.084
[♪ gentle music playing]

42:33.551 --> 42:35.553
[insects chirring]

42:38.597 --> 42:40.599
[waterfall rushing]

42:54.321 --> 42:57.241
[Dina] Okay, so... F.

42:58.242 --> 43:00.953
[Ellie]
F. Fa-fa-fa-fa-fa.

43:01.996 --> 43:03.663
- Fleetwood Mac.
- Nope.

43:03.664 --> 43:04.831
What?
What do you mean, "no"?

43:04.832 --> 43:06.583
- It's my opinion.
- Yeah, well,

43:06.584 --> 43:09.795
your opinion is wrong
because Frank Zappa exists.

43:10.838 --> 43:12.005
[Ellie] Hmm.

43:12.006 --> 43:14.340
[Dina]
Okay, so, G.

43:14.341 --> 43:16.009
[Ellie]
Uh, Green Day.

43:16.010 --> 43:18.429
[Dina]
No, you're wrong.
It's Guns N' Roses.

43:22.308 --> 43:25.101
[Ellie] Mm.
Ozzy Osbourne.

43:25.102 --> 43:27.353
[Dina]
Nice! Double points.

43:27.354 --> 43:30.857
So, L-M-N-O... P.

43:30.858 --> 43:33.401
[Ellie] Are you seriously gonna
make me do the entire alphabet?

43:33.402 --> 43:36.530
We don't have to.
I'm incredibly flexible.

43:37.656 --> 43:39.240
Lemme see, new topic...

43:39.241 --> 43:41.367
- Or silence.
- Got one.

43:41.368 --> 43:42.785
First person you killed.

43:42.786 --> 43:44.245
Jesus, really?

43:44.246 --> 43:46.205
[Dina] Yeah, fun stories
of childhood.

43:46.206 --> 43:48.750
Okay, well, the first one's
too fucked up,

43:48.751 --> 43:51.044
but I can tell you
the second one.

43:51.045 --> 43:52.046
I accept.

43:53.631 --> 43:56.132
It was a little before Joel
and I got to Jackson.

43:56.133 --> 43:59.052
In Kansas City,
he got jumped by this kid,

43:59.053 --> 44:01.180
maybe just a couple years
older than me.

44:02.056 --> 44:06.476
And I came up behind him,
raised my gun and, uh... yeah.

44:06.477 --> 44:07.769
[Dina] Oh.

44:07.770 --> 44:09.896
Sorry, Ellie.

44:09.897 --> 44:11.064
Interesting.

44:11.065 --> 44:13.025
I shoot a guy,
and you feel sorry for me?

44:14.026 --> 44:16.320
I'm just loyal like that.
[chuckles]

44:17.696 --> 44:19.405
Let me know if you see
any outcroppings

44:19.406 --> 44:21.407
- or spots with cover.
- Why?

44:21.408 --> 44:23.744
- It looks okay.
- Uh-huh.

44:25.287 --> 44:27.289
[wind whistling]

44:28.415 --> 44:30.833
[thunder crashing loudly]

44:30.834 --> 44:32.251
[Ellie]
Holy shit, that came on fast.

44:32.252 --> 44:35.088
How the fuck did you know
that was gonna happen?

44:35.089 --> 44:37.298
- I'm a witch.
- Clearly.

44:37.299 --> 44:38.592
[Dina grunts lightly]

44:41.095 --> 44:43.097
[rain pattering]

44:49.269 --> 44:50.521
[Dina sighs]

45:02.616 --> 45:04.118
Well, good night.

45:05.119 --> 45:06.245
Night.

45:10.290 --> 45:11.291
[Ellie sighs]

45:17.715 --> 45:19.717
[rain continues pattering]

45:22.594 --> 45:24.471
Okay, but I have
a stupid question.

45:31.103 --> 45:33.730
It's about New Year's Eve,

45:33.731 --> 45:35.482
and, you know...

45:36.608 --> 45:38.110
the kiss.

45:39.194 --> 45:41.154
[thunder rumbling]

45:41.155 --> 45:42.655
Okay.

45:42.656 --> 45:45.491
I mean, whatever,
you were super high.

45:45.492 --> 45:47.201
And you were drunk.

45:47.202 --> 45:48.703
Right, so it doesn't
mean anything,

45:48.704 --> 45:50.873
- if that's what you're asking.
- No, I know that.

45:51.623 --> 45:52.916
My question is...

45:54.668 --> 45:56.962
how would you rate it?

45:58.088 --> 46:01.007
- Scale of one to ten.
- No.

46:01.008 --> 46:03.342
Come on.

46:03.343 --> 46:05.511
You've kissed girls before.

46:05.512 --> 46:07.014
You're gay, I'm not.

46:07.639 --> 46:09.056
I'm just curious.

46:09.057 --> 46:10.559
I wanna know
if I'm any good at it.

46:11.435 --> 46:13.019
One to ten.

46:13.020 --> 46:15.688
[thunder continues rumbling]

46:15.689 --> 46:17.356
Okay, fine. Six.

46:17.357 --> 46:18.733
Fuck you, "six."

46:18.734 --> 46:21.861
- That's not bad.
- That sucks!

46:21.862 --> 46:23.279
- What?
- [scoffs]

46:23.280 --> 46:25.073
For the record,
I don't believe you.

46:26.366 --> 46:29.328
Well, you asked,
and I told you.
I'm sorry.

46:30.537 --> 46:33.539
You can go back to Jesse.

46:33.540 --> 46:34.917
I already did.

46:35.876 --> 46:37.919
Well, there you have it.

46:37.920 --> 46:39.462
[sighs]

46:39.463 --> 46:41.507
[rain continues pattering]

46:46.720 --> 46:49.096
[thunder rumbles softly]

46:49.097 --> 46:51.016
Does he ever strike you
as sad?

46:52.142 --> 46:53.894
Jesse? Yeah.

46:56.313 --> 46:57.898
Has he ever told you why?

46:59.316 --> 47:00.317
[Dina] No.

47:03.529 --> 47:06.072
But I think deep inside,
that's just how he is.

47:06.073 --> 47:08.075
[thunder continues]

47:09.785 --> 47:12.746
- At least, I hope that's why.
- Why would you hope that?

47:17.751 --> 47:19.670
Well, because if
it's not that...

47:21.380 --> 47:22.673
then it's me.

47:27.553 --> 47:29.471
Well, good night.

47:30.472 --> 47:31.598
Night.

47:41.483 --> 47:42.609
Ellie?

47:44.820 --> 47:46.613
I wasn't that high.

47:51.910 --> 47:53.953
[birdsong]

47:53.954 --> 47:56.999
[♪ gentle music playing]

47:59.710 --> 48:02.254
- [Ellie] How much further?
- [Dina] Close.

48:03.422 --> 48:05.631
Maybe ten miles?

48:05.632 --> 48:07.800
In theory, we'll come out
near Highway Five,

48:07.801 --> 48:09.552
- just north of the city.
- Whoa.

48:09.553 --> 48:11.388
- [insects buzzing]
- [Shimmer chortles]

48:15.726 --> 48:19.146
[♪ ominous music playing]

48:28.655 --> 48:30.073
He was running away.

48:32.117 --> 48:34.327
[Dina]
What's that symbol?

48:34.328 --> 48:36.246
[Ellie] I don't know,
I've never seen it before.

48:41.168 --> 48:43.170
[insects buzzing]

48:48.592 --> 48:50.176
[Ellie]
A lot of different calibers.

48:50.177 --> 48:51.720
I don't think this was FEDRA.

48:53.764 --> 48:54.848
Dina.

48:56.558 --> 48:58.185
- Dina?
- [leaves rustling]

48:59.102 --> 49:00.394
- [Dina] Move.
- [gasps]

49:00.395 --> 49:02.439
[Dina retching]

49:03.899 --> 49:05.901
[retching continues]

49:06.902 --> 49:08.987
- You okay?
- Mm-hmm. It's just...

49:09.905 --> 49:11.156
Mm.

49:13.325 --> 49:14.785
[Dina retching]

49:26.755 --> 49:28.840
[insects buzzing]

49:32.886 --> 49:34.888
[♪ ominous music continues]

50:05.168 --> 50:06.712
- Doing okay?
- Mm-hmm.

50:07.713 --> 50:10.798
- [sighs]
- Yeah, I'm sorry,
it's just, uh,

50:10.799 --> 50:12.217
that's never happened before.

50:13.802 --> 50:15.011
I think it was the smell.

50:15.012 --> 50:16.638
It wasn't easy
to look at either.

50:20.183 --> 50:22.268
If this was fucking them,

50:22.269 --> 50:24.646
if Abby and her crew
did this to people...

50:25.814 --> 50:27.190
to kids?

50:31.153 --> 50:32.362
Yeah.

50:36.116 --> 50:37.284
Let's go.

50:43.915 --> 50:46.918
[♪ somber music playing]

50:51.089 --> 50:53.091
[trees softly creaking]

51:02.642 --> 51:03.727
[Shimmer chortles]

51:07.773 --> 51:09.191
We're close now.

51:31.671 --> 51:33.673
[Shimmer grunting]

51:38.970 --> 51:40.513
[Dina] It's quiet.

51:40.514 --> 51:42.808
Yeah. Too quiet.

51:44.309 --> 51:47.270
- Curtis or Viper?
- Both, in all four movies.

51:50.774 --> 51:52.400
[Dina]
Nine more miles.

51:54.152 --> 51:55.445
Nine more.

51:56.446 --> 51:57.823
[clicking tongue]

52:01.076 --> 52:04.079
[♪ soft, dramatic music playing]

52:17.676 --> 52:18.760
Wow.

52:19.594 --> 52:21.972
Fucking Seattle.
Pretty.

52:24.933 --> 52:26.685
Plus, no one's shooting at us.

52:27.519 --> 52:30.312
[bird squawking]

52:30.313 --> 52:32.190
I guess there aren't
that many Wolves.

52:33.400 --> 52:35.360
There's about to be
a whole lot less.

52:37.821 --> 52:39.071
Curtis or Viper?

52:39.072 --> 52:40.573
What?

52:40.574 --> 52:42.658
No, that was just me.

52:42.659 --> 52:44.452
I was trying to sound
like a badass.

52:47.038 --> 52:48.623
You don't need to try.

53:08.852 --> 53:10.478
[soldier] [over radio]
Manny.

53:11.354 --> 53:12.606
Yeah, go ahead.

53:14.608 --> 53:16.192
- [radio beeps]
- We're moving up to the FOB.

53:16.193 --> 53:18.278
All clear between
checkpoint three and five?

53:22.032 --> 53:24.200
Told me to watch
six and eight.

53:24.201 --> 53:26.786
Now, they want fuckin'
three and five.

53:28.288 --> 53:29.830
[soldier] [on radio]
Manny, you copy?

53:29.831 --> 53:32.792
Just give me
a fuckin' second. Jesus.

53:37.464 --> 53:39.965
You're all good.
You can move up.

53:39.966 --> 53:41.551
[water dripping]

53:47.766 --> 53:50.769
[vehicle rumbling]

54:19.673 --> 54:21.675
[footfall marching]

54:24.052 --> 54:27.055
[♪ dramatic music playing]

54:49.995 --> 54:52.998
[♪ soft music playing]

55:15.687 --> 55:19.107
♪

56:00.065 --> 56:02.067
[♪ music fades out]
